sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Fusulinida (Triticites, Pseudoschwagerina, Sphaeroschwagerina, Zellia, Robustoschwagerina); Nummulina antiquior (Fig. 309); Thompson's figured genera via the generative model morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py, docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib, morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Fusulinida (Triticites, Pseudoschwagerina, Sphaeroschwagerina, Zellia, Robustoschwagerina); Nummulina antiquior (Fig. 309); Thompson's figured genera via the generative model specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean; output: docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_comparison.png; organism: Fusulinida (Triticites, Pseudoschwagerina, Sphaeroschwagerina, Zellia, Robustoschwagerina); Nummulina antiquior (Fig. 309); Thompson's figured genera via the generative model; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, lean 4.35.0, lockfile requirements.lock.txt (NOT the versions used here; the versions actually used are stamped in t1917_029_metrics.json#environment); claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 591-598: chambers/whorls in continued proportion lie on a logarithmic spiral; von Moller's Fusulina whorls in ratio ~1.5 (half-whorl 1.225, alpha ~86 deg); van Iterson's Triloculina 1.323; Rhumbler's Pulvinulina ~1.187 with a 'small secondary fluctuation'; constant volume ratio from growth proportional to existing mass. | Thompson (1917) pp. 601-605: shells differ in constant angle (rate of growth) and in chamber form/overlap; rotaline, Miliolid, Nodosarian, Textularian, Orbitolitid forms are all logarithmic-spiral cases that pass into one another by continuous gradations.; reconstructed_in_script: Discrete similar-chamber generative model (centres r0 rho^k at angle k d, radii a0 rho^k, screw translation T) with a0 = (W-1)/2 and d = 22.5 deg chosen to mimic Fig. 309; chamber overlap and a0 are not source parameters. | Per-specimen log-linear fits of test DIAMETER vs half-whorl stage (PCA frame from the mid-ontogeny outline; longest segment across the 14 two-magnification breaks); BIC vs arithmetic growth; CV and early/mid/late-third drift with Kruskal-Wallis; bootstrap CIs; KS of residuals; Monte-Carlo (normal-null) gap test; thresholds r >= 0.98, 80 %, CV <= 0.15, drift <= 10 %, +/-0.05, p >= 0.05. | CV whorl-wall radii: proloculus pins from the reference JSON (refined +/-6 px for the photograph), sector-median radial profiles, prominence/intensity thresholds 0.06/0.33 (dark walls) and 0.12/0.55 (bright engraving walls); the wall count and the exclusion of the proloculus wall (r < 90 px in Fig. 309) are analyst choices.; transfer_boundary: Dryad outlines are whorl-level axial sections of Late Paleozoic fusulinids in pixels; septal-chamber-level claims (Miliolidae, rotaline forms) are tested only through Thompson's printed tables and the generative model. | n = 1 photograph (640 x 480 px, ~6 whorls per side) and n = 1 engraving (oblique, shaded) for the CV estimates; their W values carry +/-0.10 and +/-0.18 spreads and are consistency checks, not population estimates.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that the growth ratio is physiologically caused by mass-proportional growth (E4 is proved algebraically, not tested). | Does not claim the verdict generalises beyond fusulinids plus one Nummulina engraving; the MIXED verdict is driven by the pseudoschwagerine inflation phase, which Shi (2021) describes as a heterochronic novelty. | Does not claim the KS rejection (p = 7e-4) refutes the law: with 1364 residuals the test detects the S-shaped pseudoschwagerine trajectories and digitisation outliers, i.e. the same deviation that fails T2.]; other sources: On Growth and Form — Ch. XII The Spiral Shells of the Foraminifera (pp. 587-611, Figs. 308-317) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, Die spiral-gewundenen Foraminiferen des russischen Kohlenkalks <https://archive.org/details/diespiralgewund00mlgoog>, Mathematische und mikroskopisch-anatomische Studien ueber Blattstellungen, nebst Betrachtungen ueber den Schalenbau der Miliolinen <https://archive.org/details/mathematischeund00iter>, Geometric analysis of shell coiling: general problems <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301992>, File:Fusulinid.jpg — fusulinid axial thin section (CC BY-SA 2.5, ja:User:NEON) <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fusulinid.jpg>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02266718>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
            <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
